        "**Residual plots (Figure 4)**\n",
        "\n",
        "Graphically, the residuals are centered at zero, but the distribution widens as predicted poverty increases. Counties predicted to have a poverty rate of about 10% show a small error, while those predicted to be 20% or higher show a much larger error. Regarding the bachelor's degree ratio, the residuals are also distributed around 0, showing no distinct curve. The largest lag occurs in low-education counties (10–20%). These counties have much higher poverty rates than the model predicted. Overall, the linear form seems valid, but the constant variance assumption does not hold.\n",
