        "*Your words here.*\n",
        "\n",
        "For the bachelor's degree holding rate coefficient to have a causal meaning, it must remain unrelated to other factors affecting education-related poverty even after controlling for state, rural-urban type, and median age. However, this is unlikely to be true. This means that a lower poverty rate may in part contribute to higher education levels, as college graduates are more likely to move to counties with better job opportunities.\n",
