        "\n",
        "Therefore, this coefficient should be interpreted as a conditional association rather than a causal relationship. Within the same state, among counties with the same rural-to-urban type and median age, a 1 percentage point increase in the proportion of bachelor’s degree holders was associated with an average 0.19 percentage point decrease in the poverty rate. This graph shows how education is associated with poverty in each U.S. county, but it does not indicate what changes would occur if the proportion of college graduates in a county were increased.\n",
